# ccc search — Daemon Behavior

`ccc search` requires the cocoindex daemon running.

| Fact | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Cold-start | First query after daemon start ~6 s (SBERT load). Use a ≥120 s timeout on the first call of a session. |
| Steady-state | ~7 s / query on this project (499 MB vector DB). |
| **No parallelism** | Do NOT run multiple `ccc search` in parallel — SBERT + SQLite are shared; parallel calls serialize and thermally load the laptop. Run sequentially. |
| Daemon lifecycle | `ccc daemon status` to check; `ccc daemon restart` if hung / "Failed to connect". |
| If search hangs | Daemon alive but overloaded on the large DB → `ccc daemon restart`, retry. |
| Default model | `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, 384-dim; CUDA on this machine. |

## Internals
Query → SBERT embed (384-dim) → SQLite `vec0` ANN KNN over `target_sqlite.db` → top-k by cosine → CLI/MCP.
Chunks: 1000 chars, 150 overlap. Default limit 5, max 100 (paginate via `offset`).
`refresh_index=True` by default in MCP (incremental re-walk); set `False` for repeat queries on unchanged code.
`paths=` filter falls back to a **full scan** (slower on big DB); `languages=` uses the partitioned ANN index (fast).

## Optimization
| Strategy | How | Benefit |
|----------|-----|---------|
| Language filter | `languages=["c","python"]` | partitioned ANN, no full scan |
| Small limit | `limit=5` + `offset` | less transfer |
| `refresh_index=False` | repeated queries | skips file walk |
| Warm-up | one dummy query at session start | subsequent queries steady-state |

Two-layer file filtering: `.cocoindex_code/settings.yml` include/exclude + recursive `.gitignore` stacking.
Shrink the DB by tightening `exclude_patterns` in `settings.yml`, then `ccc index --reindex`.
